{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they shall say.</b> That is, they shall answer: it is fitting that He did so to them, for they entered into the covenant of the Holy One, blessed be He, of their own will and afterward forsook Him. But the other nations did not enter into a covenant with Him, and He is not concerned about them. And from this they will justify the judgment upon them and acknowledge that it was through their own transgressions that YHWH uprooted them from upon their land, because they violated the covenant that they accepted — which the other nations did not accept. And thus Ezekiel said: ״העולה היא על רוחכם היו לא תהיה שאתם אומרים נהיה כגוים וכמשפחות האדמה לשרת עץ ואבן חי אני נאם ה' אם לא ביד חזקה ובחמה שפוכה אמלוך עליכם ואביא אתכם במסורת הברית״ — that is, because you are My people, bound in the covenant, not they. And they say: every such wrath — let the Merciful One be wrathful upon us and thereby deliver us."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:32.840505591Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}